      "truth": "NOT_REACHABLE",
      "rationale": "loud.Run calls Parse. A loud value is stored in a package-level `any` and only printed with %T, which calls no method. The only interface call, r.Run, is made on r = newRunner(), which always returns quiet{} (same method name and signature). No loud.Run call executes, so Parse is never called. Designed so the symbol can stay in the binary while no path exists."
